1
00:00:00,035 --> 00:00:05,724
Matthews story begins and ends with a promise.  Near the beginning, in Matthew chapter one, we are told:

2
00:00:05,979 --> 00:00:14,687
“And they will call Him Immanual” – which means, “god with us.” Then, at the very end of the book, the risen Jesus leaves his disciples with these words:

3
00:00:14,838 --> 00:00:32,067
“And surely I am with you always, even to the end of the age”.  From the beginning of Matthew to the very last words of Jesus, the promise remains the same: God with us. Matthew begins with Immanuel - and ends with “I am with you always.” And everything in between shows us what it means for God to be with us.

4
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:35,434
From His coming to His mission, Jesus is with His people.

